## Scaffold the generated repository

- [ ] Export `LZ_RENDERED_PATH` with the reviewed renderer output.
- [ ] Export `LZ_SCAFFOLD_TARGET` with a separate local working-tree path.
- [ ] Export `LZ_SCAFFOLD_EVIDENCE` with a protected evidence directory.
- [ ] Run `pwsh ./scaffold-copy.ps1` without `-Apply`; it is plan-only by
  default.
- [ ] Review `scaffold-plan.json` and confirm it targets
  `{{FACTORY-RAW:computed.repositorySlug}}`, branch
  `{{FACTORY-RAW:computed.defaultBranch}}`, and the approved
  `{{FACTORY-RAW:github.visibility}}` visibility.
- [ ] Confirm the manifest SHA-256 and exact file list match the approved
  renderer output.
- [ ] Authenticate GitHub CLI for repository creation and default-branch push.
- [ ] If the target is non-empty, review it and set
  `LZ_SCAFFOLD_FORCE=true`; the builder preserves a timestamped sibling backup.
- [ ] Set `LZ_SCAFFOLD_CREATE_REPOSITORY=false` if the repository must already
  exist, or `LZ_SCAFFOLD_PUSH=false` for a local-only commit.
- [ ] Optionally set `LZ_SCAFFOLD_REMOTE_URL` and
  `LZ_SCAFFOLD_COMMIT_MESSAGE`, and set `LZ_SCAFFOLD_BRANCH` to override the
  update PR branch.
- [ ] If the repository already exists, use a clean clone of
  `{{FACTORY-RAW:computed.defaultBranch}}` as `LZ_SCAFFOLD_TARGET`; the builder
  pushes an update branch and opens a draft PR instead of pushing the protected
  default branch.
- [ ] Set `LZ_SCAFFOLD_APPLY=true`, then run `./scaffold-copy.sh` or
  `pwsh ./scaffold-copy.ps1 -Apply`.
- [ ] Preserve and review `scaffold-plan.json`, `scaffold-audit.json`, and any
  `*.lz-backup-*` directory.
- [ ] Read back the remote default branch, compare the commit and managed files
  with `scaffold-audit.json`, and approve the first generated-repository PR
  checks before any Terraform apply.

